Security:
- No severe exploitable authz/injection issue observed in this diff.
- Notable security/spec concern: API key hashing uses unsalted SHA-256 instead of bcrypt (lower defense-in-depth vs requirement, though keys are high entropy).

Next actions (high impact):
1. Wire inbound message events to webhook delivery path (on business-targeted inbound replies), include retry-attempt logging and status persistence.
2. Add `GET /api/platform/billing` and fix Stripe mapping by attaching `subscription_data.metadata` (or robustly resolving client via Checkout Session/customer linkage in webhook handlers).
3. Replace API key hash storage/verification with bcrypt (or Argon2), and implement metadata-driven docs generation so `/api-platform` reflects actual route schemas automatically.

